{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>On the two ends of the breastplate.</b> These are its two bottom corners, on the right and on the left." "<b>On its band that is toward the side of the ephod, inward.</b> Here are two signs for you: the first — that he places them at the two ends of its bottom, which is opposite the ephod, for its top is not opposite the ephod, since it is close to the neck while the ephod is placed on his waist. And he gave another sign: that he should not fix them on the side of the breastplate facing outward, but on the side facing inward, as it says בָּיְתָה — and that side is toward the ephod, since the priest dons the ephod as his belt and the sash is folded in front of the priest over his waist, and part of his belly is on this side and that up to opposite the ends of the breastplate, and its ends rest upon it."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:16.714004944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}